 "sourceNotes": [
  "Issue #403 first adult MPFB2 migration slice: the 19-slot Anny nurse/spouse pair is replaced by two MPFB2 adults generated from the tracked Anny references. The Anny GLBs stay on disk as comparators.",
  "gender/muscle/weight/proportions/cupsize/firmness remain MPFB defaults — only age + height are driven by reference measurement this slice.",
  "Exact MADR 0051 §5 landmark match (shoulder, girths, limb lengths) is anny-mpfb-landmark-compare's follow-on; NOT claimed here.",
  "Family-class body is a different bake from the nurse-class body: different reference (1.66 m vs 1.76 m), different macro height (0.5 vs 0.5827), different wardrobe/iris/hair — two distinct identities.",
  "Baked 2026-08-14 from this worktree with all provider-cache assets staged locally (garments, hair, iris).",
  "Rebaked 2026-08-14 (medical wardrobe): same reference/role, scalp RULE now fires — `scalp_placeholder_retired_for` suppresses the placeholder `openclinxr_mesh_native_scalp_hair_surface` shell wherever a fitted hair mesh exists (e4880c99). Same wardrobe: toigo t-shirt (muted_rose), cortu_cargo_pants (CC0 ledger row; named-uuid GARMENT_PAGE_CC0_OVERRIDE because its `.mhclo` declares CC0 on the author line, not a `# license` line), toigo_mj_cloth_shoes, toigo_curled_under_bob hair. scalpTris=0, hairTris=2852 measured on the exported GLB.",
  "2026-09-03 #0 (fleet chest-anchor separation): separate_chest_anchor_joints.mjs mirrored breast.L / breast.R to x = +/- 0.085 m (was 0.00000 both, one midline point that made every rightChestSurface goal aim at the sternum). Producer traced to the MPFB addon rig data (CUBE head on joint-spine-1, x=0); the correction is a post-bake stage. The translation keyframes of both joints were moved with the rest nodes so clips cannot pin the anchors back onto the midline. y/z untouched; skin, meshes, materials, other joints and rotation/scale channels unchanged. Report: tools/openclinxr/evidence/chest-anchor-joints/mpfb-family-partner-adult.json. Gate: tools/openclinxr/evidence/every-shipped-rig-has-two-chest-anchors.test.ts (3 passed).",
  "2026-09-12 clothing_consume: replaced the 2,789-tri body-derived cargo cover shell with pants02 elvs_jeans_bootcut fitted via ClothesService.fit_clothes_to_human on the live MPFB hm08 basemesh (macros live, mhclo vertex bindings). Source mens_elv_jeans1f.obj 2,854 faces; shipped lower 5,708 tris (exact x2). LOWER_GATE covers raycast 0.9362. Waist meet gapped 0 / min +5.0 mm. Nurse 2,704 and street 5,708 unchanged. outputSha256 0b1b9c991e11… / 8,151,256 B -> 354624a6c76c… / 10,414,636 B.",
  "2026-09-12 clothing_consume cloth_offset: covering-library lower no longer snapped to CLOTH_STANDOFF_M after mhclo fit (materialize_mpfb_humanoid_candidate.py covering-library else-branch). Family-partner rebaked --reference ed_chest_pain_spouse_adult --actor-role family; meshopt --simplify-ratio 0.4 --simplify-error 0.001 --simplify-only; chest-anchor 0.085 m; CC-BY notice. Lower still 5,708 tris. Pants standoff p5 3.848 / med 10.637 / p95 51.463 mm (was 14.464 / 15.000 / 15.027). Nurse and street not rebaked.",
  "2026-09-20: garment-provenance-stamp extras on remaining garments. Geometry unchanged. outputSha256/outputBytes re-recorded.",
  "2026-10-30 ci-w11 D3 (chest-anchor re-separation, post-bake stage, not rebake): repair mode: rest already +-0.085 from #0; restored 2 openclinxr_retarget_walk_source keyframes per breast joint from midline to rest (walk graft 91aa4b5d3 had re-pinned them after the #0 run). Rest TRS untouched. Tool: tools/openclinxr/asset-pipeline/anny/separate_chest_anchor_joints.mjs (half-span 0.085, uniform with nurse known-good 1f5519d2).",
  "2026-10-30 ci-w11 D1 (orphan prune, not rebake): gltf-transform prune 4.3.0, same tool and flags as #555. Removed unreferenced mpfb-family-partner-adult.skin-normal (1091596 B). File 10529116 -> 9277296 B. Bound invariants held: boundTextures 5, boundBytes 4754841, meshes 10, materials 17, tris 39974, joints 137, animations 3.",
  "2026-11-04 st-vitdark r2: post-export CIELAB dark-skin remap of the skin baseColor only; Vitruvian light/African Face maps supply Lab statistics, not projected pixels; geometry/rig/animations and every non-skin image remain byte-identical.",
  "2026-11-04 st-vitdark r3: render-defect correction in the post-export CIELAB skin remap; feather tails cross feature boundaries and lip/lid chroma uses a bounded-detail target field instead of a single per-feature delta; geometry/rig/animations and every non-skin image remain byte-identical.",
  "2026-11-04 st-vitdark r9: restores the byte-identical r3 CIELAB remap, then applies one C1 output-luminance soft knee below the light bake's own darkest UV-covered texel by scaling linear RGB; geometry/rig/animations and every non-skin image remain byte-identical.",
  "2026-11-05 st-vitbrow r4: post-export fitted scalp-hair and eyebrow baseColorFactor now resolve from the case-authored hair_color token; BIN/image bytes, geometry, rig, animations, eyes, eyelashes, and skin remain unchanged.",
  "2026-11-05 st-vitrough r4: appended a subject-derived packed roughness map (G) relative to the shipped 0.78 baseline, with a derived one-G-count inside feather before scalp and lower-lid exclusions; baseColor, geometry, rig, animations, and all pre-existing buffer views remain byte-identical."
